Cameras: OH's camera HDI for the OnePlus 6, first camera the rear Sony IMX376K (kernel patches 0008-0010 of the
staged topic provide the drivers). Not yet run on the phone; the camera targets compile in an isolated build of this tree.

The port's camera/ directory was a Unisoc (wukong100) copy that nothing in the build depended on, and it would
not have worked if wired (Unisoc part, sensor classes and adapter, sprd codecs, rk3568 pipeline node names).
- camera/vdi_impl/v4l2: an rk3568-style V4L2 VDI in the board group (part qualcomm_products): the device
  manager lists one camera, imx376 (CAMERA_FIRST = lcam001); the pipeline uses the software nodes of OH's
  USB-camera VDI (scale, JPEG codec, exif, face) instead of rk3568's RK* nodes.
- camera/camss_setup: /vendor/bin/camss_setup, run once by init (service camss_setup, started in the boot
  job): waits for the sensor to bind, enables msm_csiphy1 -> msm_csid0 -> msm_vfe0_rdi0 and sets the sensor's
  current format (code and size: the Bayer order follows its flips) on those pads. CAMSS has no ISP, the
  graph carries raw Bayer end to end; OH's V4L2 adapter (drivers/peripheral 0002) converts it.
- cfg/ueventd.config: camera_host may open /dev/media* and /dev/v4l-subdev* (format of the RDI subdev,
  exposure and gain on the sensor subdev).
- modules: the camera modules are installed (modules_path_194.gni) and loaded at boot (modules.load).

